      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-10_WidnesExaminer_art0048" n="art0048">
        <head>:X A. E .</head>
        <p>:X A. E .</p>
        <p>OCTOBER 10th, 1896.</p>
        <p>_..ve</p>
        <p>political sensation of 9 s the resignation by TAII CRY of the leadership of resignation is, a /vault of . $</p>
        <p>Jr the letter in-• which ct, which is addrassed to .11 f Liberal whip, Lord Re at course of events makes) air. I find myself in apr a considerable mass ef e Eastern Question, al nion with Mr. GALDS always exercise a mal. ty, while scarcely fro) 3xplicit support. This irds Mr. GLADSTONE/ in saying this I ootnplsw; ily that I should apees:ol id try the faith of LiOil er, is above and beyondli . When I speak, whicil 0 ,eak my mind,, and se/ party. Under these eV II ;he party and myself til'l 1 eader, but as a free notify to youthat the OA is far as I am concern°"f d I resume my libertited 1r does undoubtedly 0 the air" so far tioi concerned. The resigeAdo: lected, though perhaps 1104 tuistances it is not surPr till 3 . There can be no has not been in liat,v I, e members of the tall vith the Armenian ities have moved the I)l9iii it has not been moved f 0 not Liberals alone, hsreo f,, mder special obligati`"ba Dori tion of Turkey, and tlIP' / nit() diplomatic plede, 0 ' nanity, something 511°1il 4pv- i , lonians from a cruel InoP too that while this CO tll° neither is it withetioed tbstautial relief. It is °A of relief that the " diffoviii Liberal Party, to wlliet's, s sprung up. Lord P2s 0) A , the utmost abliorrellej D' and indeed has expos° p, point as strongly its 10,11 ii ;her hand he appears tal,l v nto sheer inactivity i;rottli ices that might tuise t Yi ton by this countrY• le e di 0' elit expressions ox it., n of lectors and other „ir „ 0-41 ;tinct tendency to into which so manY ,at their head, have l‘ovoos f,„rcl out enthusiasm. -'-'" • a 1,1 01 horoughly convince ill/ direct intervention inf. jos API this country. 12-1 - ss'A ureign Office hillisell'o. ilrA ample infornastineil )pinion than is In the other hand) DO lat agitation wilic'h bet • idy point to the fac,..teo(3ll y had a decidedly ,i' to tainly not broliqoruk ful cataclysm, an oot )ther hand done</p>
