        <p>The fol'owing persons were fined for sending their chil- dren irregularly to lichen; Kills. Surrey-tit., ad- journed for a week ; Arthur Haddock. 17. Surrey-st.. ss. ; , Job Neil Handley-st.. 55,; Owen Roberts. Okel-st., 58 ; I Joseph Wakefield, 46, Lock ss. ; Thomas Watson, 48, Lock-st.. 58 ; James ClAfrn-d..none Hills, 55.; Rmma Moore. adpurned for a week ; Thomas Jones. 115.Sarrey- st., 59. John Saunders 131 esm re-st.. ordered to attend National School : Henry Burton. 43, Camendish-st., ss. Mr. T. Bowyer. School Bo•irA officer. prosecuted. DBUNK. Moff ft was ehirged with being drunk and disorderly in Gre.m way-road on Saturday.—Pinedss.and cots. HEAVY SENTENCE ON AN OUT-LOISOUR.—SoIina Giblin was charged with lodging in an unoccupied house on the 4th Inst.. P.O Hughes croveil the case, and Giblin was sea- tenced to three months' imprisonment with hard labour. TusanAT —Before Mr. J. W Lightburn and Mr. J, Nor ran. DRITNE.—Fred Chen was charged with being drunk and disor erlv in •liirreY-3t. Ma previous night. Prisoner's wife stated that he hot abcce £3O lett him a few weeks ago, and he had loan At-Ong no'hine only &amp;inking ever since.—The migistrat.s impwed a fine of ss. and costs.</p>
