        <p>F' 'ISH AT WORSLEY'S, "THE PANTHEON," GAYTWORN, MANCHESTER. HIGH-CLAoS SECOND-HAND FURNITURE, FURNITURE BY JAMES LAMB. GOODALL, GARNETT, GILLOWS, STARKEY AND NIELD, HENRY OGDEN , AND SONS, DOVESTON, DYSON, MAPLE, AND SCHOOLB RED. CRUSHING DEFEAT OF HIGH PRICES. -AVEEKLY CHA T.-We respectfully draw attention this week to the various lots we are specially advertising. The terms of purchase will include delivery, and a guarantee for each lot for five years. The list we give be'ow forms only a small and infinitesimal part of the bargains we have on view at "The Pantheon." What we are advertising to-day is an illustration of what we can do, and what we have on show. Inspection invited. COMPLETE HOUSES OF FURNITURE. kol Lot 1. Splendid House of Furniture, containing Din- ing-room, Drawing-reena, Sitting-room, Kitchen, and four Bedrooms. Cost £2lO. Our price, £B5. Lot 2. Excellent House of Furniture for a Working-man for £2O, consisting of a solid kahogany Dining-room Suite, Dining-table, Sideboard, Carpet, Brass Fender and Brasses, Kitchen Chairs, Table, Oilcloth, Rug. Fender, Ashpan. Flee- irons ' - Bedroom Suite, Brass and Enamelled Bedstead. Mat- tress, Bed, Bolster and Pillows, Carpet, Toilet Ware, and side sundries. A Wonderful bargain. hot 3. An Exceptional Offer. We can offer a splendid Bargain in a House of Furniture for £4O. The Furniture is all well-mede, very stylish, and equal to new. The Dining- room is furnished in Solid Oak and Morocco. The Sitting- room in Solid Mahogany. There is also Kitchen Furniture and two Bedrooms very handsomely furnished. A complete list will be sent on application, pest free. We have en view complets Houses of Furuiture from £lO up to £5OO. Full and complete list of each will be sent post free, on application. DI NI NG-ROOM FURNITURE. Lot 50. Second-hand Spanish Mahogany Dining-room Suite, in Morocco, handsomely carved for £B. Lot 51 Fecond-haad American Wsonut Dining-room Suite in leather, £4 15s. Lot 52: Second-hand Brown Oak Dining-room Suite, in velvet, 5 guineas Lot 53. An eotraordinary Massive Dining-room Suite, in Spanish Mahogany, consisting of a spoon-back Suite, of Couch, two Noisy Chairs, and six Single Chairs, upholstered ' In Morocco. Magnificent Spanish Mahogany Sideboard to match, with lofty plate-glass back, most beautifully carved in good preservation. 10ft. DI ing-table on massive carved sup- ports. This lot is worth to-day £lOO. and cost over £2OO when new, and will be sold a bargain for £4O. Lot 54. Fine old Spanish Sideboard, 7ft. 61n. long, in Spanish mahogany, cost £7O. Lot 56. Second hand Dining-roein Suite complete, with Sideboard, Table. and Overmantel. the suite upholstered in Morocco. Cost £B6. Price sBl guineas. Lot 57 Good Second-hand Dining-room Suite, of nine pieces, splendid Sideboard and Dining Table to set 10 per- sons, together with the Overmantel. Onrprice for quick sale 15 guineas. Lot 58. Magnificent Pollard Oak Dining-room Suite, suit- able for a nobleman. This Furniture is second-hand, but it is quite equal to new, having been entirely re-upholstered in Morocco ; it is in beautiful condition,and spotless throughout. The design is original, and is by a celebrated maker. The Sideboard is 7ft long, palatial in size, and beautiful in de- sign ; the wood is the very finest figured Pollard Oak. The carving Is executed in fine has relief,and is a work of art. The Suite is by Taylor and Whitfield; the carving alone must have cost a fabulous sum. Consists of very beautiful Conch. pair of Easy Chairs, and six Siagle Chairs. We can provile 12 Single Chairs if necessary. The Dining Table is 18ft long and matches the rest of the Furniture. We have not the slightest hesitation in declaring that this Furniture Is worth £5OO. Our price for the lot is £2OO. N.8.-It will be seen by the let 58 we have just described that VS OeSLISY'S must have a very extensive stook. We have just described three pieces of Furniture for £2OO, and wkile in Lot 57 we give a lot for Diningroom for 15 guineas, show- ing what a wide and Extensive Stock Worsley's have on show. We have over 100 complete Diningroom Suites on show, besides scores of odd Sideboards an i odd Dining Tables. DRAWING-ROOll FURNITURE. In this Department we have perhaps the finest selec- tion of Furniture to be seen in any house in the country. It is very difficult to select out of the bargains on view in this room a few that will convey a fair idea of their ma.otifi- cence and quality in this short paragraph ; there are such a quantity of them. We have over 100 Drawing-room Suites on show in every variety of colour and shade of upholstery. We give one or two examples :- Lot 215. Very exquisitely pretty and unique Chippendale Drawing-room Suite for £l2, perhaps the greatest marvel of any bargain that has been offered ; it is quite sufficient to say that this Suite is beautifully inlaid and covered in the meet silk tapestry. It is a second-hand suite whieh has beco re covered and re.polished, sad entirely renovated, and is now entirely equal to new. It would undoubtedly compare favourably with any hing that is being offered for £25 and £3O eleswhere. We have the Cabinet to match at the same price, £l2. This is just as beautifully made, contains numerous shelves for bric-a-brac. and splendidly fitted with bevel plates ; there is also an Overmantel, which matches. ler 3 guineas, two Occasional Tables at 18s, each, a Music Cabinet for £2 165., and Lady's Writing Table for £3 10e. ; altogether terming the prettiest collection of Chippendale furniture which has ever been on show at the price. Lots 310 to 330. A Fine Collection of 20 Second-hand Cabi- nets and Chiffoniers, from £2 lOs. up to £lO. These have been marked exceedingly low to clear, and are of the good old-fashioned make. Everyone of these are second-baud. I Lets 351 to 365 Fourteen Wonderfully Cheap Overmantels, second-hand. Some of these cost as much as £2O, We shall offer them from 30s. to £5. Lot 366. SPECIAL BARGAIN. The Prettiest. Best, and Cheapest Drawing-room Suite evsr offered. This Suite is of exceptional merit ; it consists 01 the sweetest designed Settee, and pair of lasi. Chairs, two exquisite Occasional Chairs,and two beautiful Single Chairs. The whole is very prettily in- laid w th Ivory, and upholstered in silk tapestry ; well worth 255. per yard. "he cabinet to match is of a design both weird and peculiar ;curious little columns with niches tor the display of chine,grotesque little cupboards fitted with bevelled crystals. special cover, and of peculiar shape for five o'clock tea service; two of the trickiest little tables imaginable, a peculiar and beautiful little Overmantel to match the lot, design of which is just as grotesque and curious as the rest of Furniture. This is the kind of Suite that ladies fall in love with wherever it is seen. Our price for the lot 21.,• guineas, pvißoom FURNITURE. LY WO fiSLEY'S have the Biggest Show of Bedroom Furni- ture of anyone in the United Kingdom. We are quite aware that most Houses lay claim to having the Biggest Stock, but we challenge any intending purchaser to compare by inspec- tion the Enormous Stock of Bedroom Furniture at WORS- LETO with that of any other goose in the Kingdom We have over 300 Bedroom Suites ( n show. we save just corn_ pleted another contract for 300 B di onus Suites for our stock, , and we have in process of manutacture,orders with mainline- I I hirers of bedsteads which shell bring our stock to little short of 1,0,50 I edsteacls. Out of this varied collection we select a , few sample bargains only. I SPECIAL NOTICE. You might hear a remarlc that it is I very seldom you visit WORo LEY'S but that you can pick up such a bargain that more than repays the trouble of your Lot 789. A Magnificent Pollard 'Oak BEDROOM SUITE will he told a bargain foe £l2O which originally cost £LOO. This is the finest bedroom suite in Manchester. Lot 792. • Very Handsome Bedroom Suite, smaller in size, suitable for 